**Verdicts**
- **(i) V(1x1) = 1/2:** STANDS.
- **(ii) V(1xw) ≤ w·V(1x1):** STANDS. All 7 of 7 widths qualify, and V/(w·V11) falls from 1 to 0.673 at w=64.
- **(iii) V(wxw) ≤ w²·V(1x1):** STANDS, but it is far from sharp. All 7 of 7 squares qualify, and V/(w²·V11) falls to 0.031.
- **(iv) Exponents:** the log-log slope between w=32 and w=64 is a = 0.986 for the strip and a = 1.024 for the square. So the L² norm sqrt(V) scales as w^0.493 and w^0.512, close to w^(1/2). V grows roughly with the perimeter, not the area. I did not test a pure power law, so these are local slopes, not asymptotic exponents.

